			"notes": {
				"rationale": "sog. is Duden's abbreviation of sogenannt. It is one Segment with its period and a Shorthand member whose Surface is the expansion as the phrase needs it: ein sogenannter Experte, nominative masculine singular (de/abbreviation-is-one-segment). Duden gives sogenannt no comparison forms, so the attributive Surface marks case, gender and number only (de/comparability-is-lexical). Duden gives sogenannt one sense, 'wie es genannt wird, heißt', its mocking use (deine sogenannten Freunde) included, so 🏷 holds whether or not the expert is doubted. Knowledge (#887, dev draft): sogenannt is so + genannt with no verb *sonennen, so it is not a Participial Adjective and takes no Participle Source."
